content.text:
Potential temporal dead zone: build() calls el('#target-confirm').addEventListener('click', () => choose(sel)) and `cancel` referenced in listener. `build()` is called at end after `cancel` and `handler` defined, so fine. But `build` is defined before `choose`/`cancel` const declarations; closures evaluate later. Fine.

However `update()` inside build is called at build time; `update` const defined before build. Good.

Now add CSS for `.cmd-actions`, `.battle-confirm`, `.battle-back`, `.target-cards`, `.target-actions`. Also adjust target-layer to column. Need ensure target cards layout.

Current `.target-layer` display flex gap etc. Modify:
```
.target-layer{
 position:absolute;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);bottom:max(16px,...);
 display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;padding:9px;...
 max-width:min(96vw,720px);
}
.target-cards{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;}
.target-actions{display:flex;gap:7px;}
.target-actions .battle-confirm{flex:1;}
```
Buttons:
```
.cmd-actions{display:flex;gap:6px;margin-top:8px;}
.battle-confirm,.battle-back{
  flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
  padding:9px 12px;min-height:38px;cursor:pointer;
  border:1px solid rgba(231,199,123,.55);
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(231,199,123,.18),rgba(231,199,123,.06));
  color:#fff3d3;font-size:17px;font-family:var(--body);
  transition:...;
}
.battle-confirm:hover{...}
.battle-confirm span{font-family:var(--pixel);font-size:7px;color:var(--gold);}
.battle-back{flex:0 0 auto;border-color:rgba(160,180,210,.22);background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);color:var(--muted);}
```
For command menu footer only confirm full width.

Target actions: `.target-actions .battle-confirm{flex:1}` and back.

Mobile: `.cmd-actions` maybe margin-top 6; button min-height 34; font 15.

Also target layer bottom on mobile maybe 10; fine. With actions added, height increases; could overlap command panel but z-index. Maybe set target layer bottom to `max(76px, ...)` on desktop? Let's see: command panel bottom 16 height ~226; target layer bottom 16, height cards ~50 + actions ~45 + padding = 110, so top 594; command panel top 478. Overlap area y594-704, x center. Target layer z-index 5, covers part of command panel. That's okay because target menu is modal-ish; command panel is behind. But the confirm button in target layer is visible. On mobile, command panel with-party width 62vw, target layer max 96vw, z-index 5, covers. Fine.

Maybe when target layer open, command menu is cleared? No, commandMenu cleared root before returning 'attack' (root.innerHTML=''). So command panel is empty (still border background) during target selection. Thus no overlap issue visually except empty panel. Good! For skill menu, root remains with skill list while target selection? `skillMenu` clears root via finishMenu? No, finishMenu only pops handler and resolves; it does not clear root. In commandMenu choose clears root. In skillMenu choose does not clear root. So skill list remains behind target layer. But target layer z-index 5 covers center; skill panel left. Fine. Could clear root in skill/item choose but not necessary. Maybe better to clear root when choosing skill/item to avoid stale UI. Existing behavior left it. Not part of bug.

Now CSS patch.

